# =============================================================================
# Trivy ignore list — Brew & Co.
# =============================================================================
# All entries below are vulnerabilities in npm's own internal toolchain
# packages (located at /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/ inside
# the base Node container images). These packages are used by npm itself at
# install-time and are never loaded or executed by our application at runtime.
#
# Suppressing them is the standard practice: the attack surface they represent
# does not exist in a production container where npm is not invoked.
# See: https://trivy.dev/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
# =============================================================================

# brace-expansion — npm internal dep (minimatch/glob resolution)
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152

# ip-address — npm internal dep (network address parsing for npm registry)
CVE-2026-69192

# pacote — npm internal dep (package fetching during npm install)
CVE-2026-9496

# picomatch — npm internal dep (glob pattern matching)
CVE-2026-33671

# sigstore — npm internal dep (npm provenance verification)
CVE-2026-48815

# tar — npm internal dep (tarball extraction during npm install)
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874
CVE-2026-73566
